            {
              "type": "Progress Notes",
              "title": "New Patient Visit",
              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2023-11-07T09:30",
              "body": "41-year-old man joining the practice. Feels well, no complaints today, mainly wants a doctor he can reach and a baseline checkup. Works as a sales manager for a corporate account team, a lot of driving and some air travel, sits a good part of the day.\n\nPMH: none. No chronic illnesses, no hospitalizations.\nPSH: tonsils out at age 7.\nMeds: none, no supplements.\nAllergies: none to medications.\nFamily: father with high blood pressure and type 2 diabetes. Mother with an underactive thyroid. Sister gets migraines.\nSocial: never used tobacco. Has 2-3 drinks on weekends, social. Single, lives in Westfield.\nROS: negative across systems; sleeps OK, mood good.\n\nExam: well appearing, vitals as recorded. HEENT unremarkable, TMs clear, oropharynx without lesions (tonsils surgically absent). Neck supple, no thyroid enlargement or nodes. Heart regular, no murmur. Lungs clear. Abdomen soft, nontender, no organomegaly. Extremities warm, no swelling. Neuro: cranial nerves grossly intact, face symmetric, strength and gait normal. Skin: nothing of note.\n\nPHQ-2 0.\n\nAssessment/plan:\n1. Adult health maintenance. Baseline CBC, CMP, lipids. A1c given his father's diabetes. One-time hepatitis C and HIV screening, he agrees.\n2. Immunizations: no record of a tetanus booster in at least 10 years per patient, Tdap today. Flu vaccine today.\n3. Colon cancer screening starts at 45, will plan for it then.\n4. Old records requested.\n\nFollow up for a physical next fall, or message any time."
            }
